---
title: Eggnog
servings: 6
yield: about 6 cups
tags: [cocktail, rum, christmas, winter, make-ahead]
time: 3 hours 25 minutes
source: Homemade Eggnog by Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/eggnog.html
---

In a #large bowl{}, whisk the @egg yolks{6}, @heavy cream{1 1/2%cup}, @granulated sugar{1/2%cup} and @salt{1/4%tsp} until smooth.

Bring the @whole milk{2%cup} to a gentle boil in a #medium saucepan{} over medium-high heat. Off the heat, pour it slowly into the yolks, whisking all the time.

Pour it all back into the pan and cook over medium-low heat, whisking, ~{2%minutes} to 3 minutes, until it thickens a little and reads 160 to 165°F on a #thermometer{}. Don't let it boil.

Strain it through a #fine-mesh strainer{} into a clean bowl. Whisk in the @dark rum{1/3%cup}, @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp}(scant) and @ground cinnamon{1/8%tsp}. Cool, cover, and chill at least ~{3%hours}.

Stir, ladle into glasses, and top with @heavy cream{}(whipped, optional) and a pinch of nutmeg.

> Bourbon or brandy work in place of the rum, or leave it out and pour it on the side. Keeps 3 days in the fridge.
